## Reserved resource floor for Mangrove's own control plane (mangrove.service)
## and Caddy. MemoryMin is a protection floor: under memory pressure the
## kernel will not reclaim this slice's memory in favor of
## mangrove-deployments.slice, so a runaway deployment container cannot
## starve Mangrove/SSH access to death. MemoryHigh is a soft ceiling on
## Mangrove itself (throttles rather than kills).
##
## Install: copy to /etc/systemd/system/mangrove.slice, then
## `systemctl daemon-reload`. mangrove.service and caddy.service both need
## `Slice=mangrove.slice` (see mangrove.service and caddy-mangrove-slice.conf).

[Unit]
Description=Mangrove control plane (reserved floor)
Before=slices.target

[Slice]
MemoryMin=384M
MemoryHigh=512M
CPUWeight=200
